WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.311
Welcome.

00:00:00.311 --> 00:00:05.600
In this video, you will learn about how to use the ASIN Status Report to remove or

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.909
unenroll eligible ASINs in Canada and Mexico in the Remote Fulfillment by FBA program.

00:00:11.909 --> 00:00:12.360
To

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:17.560
start, go to the Inventory menu in Seller Central and then select the Remote Fulfillment

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.976
with FBA option from the dropdown.

00:00:19.976 --> 00:00:23.600
Click on Generate Report to generate the latest version

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:24.744
of the report.

00:00:24.744 --> 00:00:28.939
When the report is ready, the download button will be activated.

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:29.320
Click

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.189
on the button to view the report.

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:34.660
On the Enrollment tab of the report, you will be able to review

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:40.640
ASIN status on your entire FBA selection, including ASINs that are enabled, eligible and

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.086
enrolled, ineligible or requires action to enable.

00:00:44.086 --> 00:00:47.040
You can unenroll enabled ASINs at

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:47.824
any point.

00:00:47.824 --> 00:00:52.528
Simply filter to ASINs labeled as Enable on the Offer Status column.

00:00:52.528 --> 00:00:52.920
Type

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:57.960
in No on the Enable Disable column under the destination marketplace you wish to unenroll

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:58.934
the offers from.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:03.480
Save the changes in your file and go back to the Manage Your Remote Fulfillment

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.150
ASINs page.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:06.160
Click on the Choose File button.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.840
Select the ASIN Status Report file you just

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:12.200
saved and upload it back into our system.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.720
Once the upload is completed successfully,

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.320
check under Results to make sure there are zero errors.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.480
The select ASINs will be unenrolled

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.768
in chosen marketplaces within 24 hours.

00:01:22.768 --> 00:01:26.200
In the future, if you want to reactivate those

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:32.360
ASINs, simply download the latest report again and type in Yes in the Enable Disable column

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:33.983
under the intended marketplaces.

00:01:33.983 --> 00:01:38.040
Upload your saved report and your offers will be reactivated

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.680
or re-enrolled within 24 hours.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.880
Thank you and happy selling!
